 "poem": "XIII. OMNES DE ILLUMINUS de\nIambis, in vestidum et mit.\n157. 'O my own poor Soul!' a Spanish lady\nSaid her, 'How couldst thou ever have pity\nOn the unhappy things that upon\nThe ground so freely fell? Thy despair\nIs as just as I've felt it must follow\nThat thy soul should sink into decay.' There\nShe drew near the grave and reached away\nA little with the hand of consolation;\nThen softly stroked to herself her faded\nAnd tender features; and, lo! - she remained",
